# Sentinel file for the EXTRACT_METADATA process `voxel_sidecar` input.
#
# Background
# ----------
# SPLIT_INPUT_FILE emits a `voxel_size.json` sidecar on the .ims / .h5 /
# .hdf5 input paths so EXTRACT_METADATA can read the Imaris HDF5 voxel
# metadata directly (TIFF tags / ImageJ metadata are unreliable for these
# formats — see repo-memory "voxel_metadata_handling"). On the .czi /
# .tif hyperstack paths and on the plain folder-of-per-timepoint-TTIFFs
# path SPLIT_INPUT_FILE never runs, so no sidecar exists.
#
# Why this sentinel exists
# ------------------------
# Nextflow DSL2 forbids `optional: true` on a *path INPUT* (it's only
# valid on a path OUTPUT). Before this sentinel existed, the EXTRACT_METADATA
# input was declared as `path voxel_sidecar, optional: true`, which Nextflow
# rejected at script-parse time with:
#
#     No such property: optional for class: nextflow.script.params.FileInParam
#     Possible solutions: options
#
# i.e. the pipeline failed at launch before any task could run. The fix
# is to ALWAYS stage a real file (either the real voxel_size.json or this
# sentinel) and let the bash-layer's existing
#
#     sidecar_path = Path('voxel_size.json')
#     if sidecar_path.exists(): ...
#
# guard handle the absence. The sentinel is named differently so the
# guard above correctly skips it as data and the script falls back to
# the user-supplied config.voxel_size / auto-detect-from-TIFF-tags path.
#
# Why the basename must differ from voxel_size.json
# -------------------------------------------------
# Nextflow stages path inputs under their basename by default. If this
# sentinel were named `voxel_size.json`, it would always exist in the
# EXTRACT_METADATA workdir (overriding the real sidecar in a -resume
# scenario where the upstream task cached an empty sidecar) and the
# bash script would happily try to JSON-decode an empty file. The .marker
# suffix keeps it out of the JSON lookup while still satisfying the
# "must stage something" contract of a DSL2 path input.
#
# Why not pass an empty Channel.value([]) instead
# -----------------------------------------------
# A Channel.value([]) emits ONE element (an empty list). Nextflow will
# still invoke EXTRACT_METADATA once, and `voxel_sidecar` becomes an
# empty list in the bash script. That technically works (the .exists()
# check fails and the script falls back), but it interacts badly with
# future refactors — e.g. any `*.json` publishDir pattern would never
# match, and Nextflow prints a warning at task start that "no files
# were staged for path input `voxel_sidecar`". The sentinel gives a
# clean success path with no warnings and a self-documenting workdir.
